WEBVTT

00:06.760 --> 00:09.480
Well, the view isn't bad.

00:10.020 --> 00:12.200
The humidity is at 32%.

00:12.200 --> 00:16.050
Atmospheric turbidity is low, too,
so you can see far into the distance.

00:16.050 --> 00:18.360
You can look down on everything from here.

00:19.190 --> 00:21.540
This residence is worthy
of one who stands at the top.

00:22.040 --> 00:24.370
Is that an okay, then?

00:24.370 --> 00:26.630
You'll live here with me?

00:26.630 --> 00:28.280
Don't be ridiculous.

00:28.280 --> 00:31.250
It would be absurd for
the four of us to live together.

00:31.250 --> 00:33.920
We only came because you called us.

00:33.920 --> 00:35.640
And that's what you wanted to discuss?

00:35.640 --> 00:36.680
No way.

00:36.680 --> 00:39.140
What? You guys are so cold.

00:42.450 --> 00:46.370
But I think it's what we need right now.

02:33.670 --> 02:36.710
Song Festa's guests tonight are...

02:33.810 --> 02:40.470
Minemori Keisuke          Tateishi Shizuka

02:36.710 --> 02:40.470
These individuals chosen to appear
in the Triple S decisive concert.

02:41.870 --> 02:42.930
STARISH!

02:46.350 --> 02:50.100
And tonight we have another special guest.

02:50.100 --> 02:53.210
Speaking of artists appearing
in the Triple S decisive concert...

02:55.080 --> 02:56.230
HEAVENS!

03:00.740 --> 03:04.370
No one told me HEAVENS
was coming on the show, too.

03:04.370 --> 03:07.700
They don't tell us everything in advance.

03:07.700 --> 03:10.220
Huh? What the hell is this?

03:10.220 --> 03:12.260
We're appearing with STARISH?

03:12.260 --> 03:17.210
Why didn't they introduce us first
when we're the best group in the universe?

03:25.480 --> 03:27.330
What is this?

03:29.020 --> 03:30.160
What's going on?

03:29.020 --> 03:31.890
What on earth is going on?!

03:33.150 --> 03:35.900
Raging Otori

03:35.900 --> 03:37.650
Raging Otori has suddenly appeared!! What will happen at the studio?!

03:36.220 --> 03:37.650
Raging Otori?

03:37.650 --> 03:41.700
Rejoice, HEAVENS and STARISH.

03:42.640 --> 03:47.370
I'm here to announce a revolutionary
project that will knock your socks off.

03:48.080 --> 03:49.750
Listen closely!

03:50.300 --> 03:56.210
HEAVENS and STARISH will be working
on a duet project together!

03:53.310 --> 03:56.210
Duet Project

03:56.210 --> 03:59.920
STARISH and HEAVENS to work on a duet project!

03:56.650 --> 03:57.910
Wh-What?

03:57.910 --> 03:59.920
A duet project?

04:00.650 --> 04:02.000
A duet...

04:02.000 --> 04:03.390
...project.

04:03.390 --> 04:04.800
What does this mean?

04:07.660 --> 04:12.020
Shining Saotome

04:07.880 --> 04:12.020
Allow me to announce the details.

04:12.020 --> 04:17.110
The members of STARISH
and HEAVENS will sing together

04:17.110 --> 04:22.570
one by one in this super dreaming plan!

04:22.880 --> 04:23.930
What?

04:23.930 --> 04:27.160
One member each from STARISH
and HEAVENS will sing together?

04:24.640 --> 04:27.820
-What a shocking announcement!

04:27.160 --> 04:28.820
What kind of plan is that?

04:28.820 --> 04:30.040
I don't believe this.

04:30.300 --> 04:31.570
The featured...

04:31.570 --> 04:34.500
Duos are...

04:34.500 --> 04:39.580
Ittoki Otoya

04:34.500 --> 04:39.620
Otori Eiichi

04:35.410 --> 04:39.630
Ittoki Otoya and Otori Eiichi.

04:39.630 --> 04:44.720
Sumeragi Kira

04:39.630 --> 04:44.720
Hijirikawa Masato

04:40.730 --> 04:44.720
Sumeragi Kira and Hijirikawa Masato.

04:44.720 --> 04:49.640
Shinomiya Natsuki

04:44.720 --> 04:49.640
Mikado Nagi

04:45.650 --> 04:49.640
Shinomiya Natsuki and Mikado Nagi.

04:49.640 --> 04:54.810
Otori Eiji

04:49.640 --> 04:54.810
Ichinose Tokiya

04:50.670 --> 04:54.810
Otori Eiji and Ichinose Tokiya.

04:54.810 --> 05:00.020
Kiryuin Van

04:54.810 --> 05:00.020
Jinguji Ren

04:56.030 --> 05:00.020
Jinguji Ren and Kiryuin Van

05:00.020 --> 05:05.150
Hyuga Yamato

05:00.020 --> 05:05.150
Kurusu Syo

05:01.030 --> 05:05.150
Hyuga Yamato and Kurusu Syo.

05:05.150 --> 05:10.410
Aijima Cecil

05:05.150 --> 05:10.410
Amakusa Shion

05:06.320 --> 05:10.410
Aijima Cecil and Amakusa Shion.

05:10.410 --> 05:14.700
These two groups are thrilling and fashionable!

05:14.700 --> 05:19.790
And through their union
is born an unprecedented project!

05:19.790 --> 05:22.630
Coming soon!

05:23.370 --> 05:25.050
A duet project?

05:25.050 --> 05:27.260
What? What is this?

05:27.260 --> 05:28.320
Trending: Japan

05:28.320 --> 05:29.220
HEAVENSSS. I've been waiting for this! I want to see it now!
Yahoooooo! Everyone's so handsome and cute, I can't stand it.
Yes, yes, yes, yes!!!
All right!!!!

05:29.220 --> 05:30.950
Duet Project

05:29.220 --> 05:30.950
Extra Innings

05:29.220 --> 05:30.950
Raging Otori

05:29.220 --> 05:30.950
Professional Baseball

05:29.220 --> 05:30.950
Shining Saotome

05:31.260 --> 05:32.590
I was so surprised.

05:32.590 --> 05:34.390
I can't believe we're
singing duets with HEAVENS.

05:34.390 --> 05:38.980
It certainly is a timely plan
for capturing the world's attention.

05:39.330 --> 05:41.950
They must be planning to simultaneously

05:41.950 --> 05:46.510
brush up our individual talents
in preparation for the decisive concert, too.

05:46.510 --> 05:48.410
But I don't like it.

05:48.410 --> 05:54.590
Yeah. Will it be possible for us to sing
with people we've hardly spoken to?

05:54.590 --> 05:58.210
But if it goes well, I'm sure it'll be tons of fun.

05:58.210 --> 06:00.260
I agree.

06:00.260 --> 06:03.230
No matter who you're singing
with, singing is always fun.

06:03.230 --> 06:05.500
No matter who you're singing with?

06:05.500 --> 06:07.760
I'm singing with Otori Eiichi!

06:10.010 --> 06:11.260
Good!

06:13.130 --> 06:15.150
Can we really get along with them?

06:16.210 --> 06:18.390
Otoya, it's all right.

06:18.730 --> 06:22.150
Let's work together to make this plan a success.

06:23.310 --> 06:24.440
Yeah.

06:25.850 --> 06:28.540
This is exactly the kind of thing
Dad would come up with.

06:28.540 --> 06:29.490
Right, Eiji?

06:29.490 --> 06:30.830
Brother.

06:30.830 --> 06:33.260
Unprecedented project, my ass.

06:33.260 --> 06:34.510
Don't make me laugh.

06:35.790 --> 06:38.270
But it could be useful.

06:38.270 --> 06:41.830
Yeah. It could be a good opportunity
to learn something about them.

06:41.830 --> 06:43.560
I don't want to know them.

06:43.560 --> 06:45.560
Shion's right.

06:45.560 --> 06:47.630
What good would knowing them do?

06:47.630 --> 06:49.690
I don't care either way.

06:49.690 --> 06:53.930
After all, our supremely super group
is going to win at the decisive concert.

07:05.440 --> 07:07.970
What the hell is this duet project?

07:08.400 --> 07:10.110
Don't worry about it.

07:10.110 --> 07:11.030
What?

07:11.430 --> 07:14.320
Nothing will affect our superiority.

07:15.100 --> 07:16.910
Do you lack confidence?

07:16.910 --> 07:19.410
What? Of course not.

07:20.180 --> 07:21.450
Bastard!

07:21.450 --> 07:22.990
Wait, wait. Guys-

07:22.990 --> 07:28.920
At the previous concert, QUARTET NIGHT was
rated higher than STARISH and HEAVENS.

07:29.870 --> 07:34.180
But when people complete, it's not just
ability that determines the outcome.

07:34.180 --> 07:36.990
That's right. Ai-Ai's right.

07:36.990 --> 07:42.440
Isn't that why we started living together?

07:44.080 --> 07:50.520
STARISH and HEAVENS' strength is built
on the bonds between their members.

07:51.050 --> 07:53.490
We need to work on building our own bonds.

07:53.490 --> 07:56.550
Don't ever enter my private quarters. Got it?

07:56.550 --> 07:58.370
Why are you saying it like that?

07:59.880 --> 08:01.330
No one's listening.

08:01.330 --> 08:02.850
I'd never go in your room.

08:02.850 --> 08:04.170
You stay out of mine.

08:04.170 --> 08:05.960
How dare you speak so rudely?

08:06.380 --> 08:08.770
Could you two stop fighting over everything?

08:08.770 --> 08:09.300
What?

08:09.860 --> 08:11.430
Man, shut up.

08:22.270 --> 08:23.690
Some are missing...

08:23.690 --> 08:24.800
Who did it?

08:25.780 --> 08:29.070
Oh, I borrowed some while I was cooking.

08:29.070 --> 08:30.620
Don't use my things without asking!

08:30.620 --> 08:32.420
You're awfully anal, aren't you?

08:32.420 --> 08:34.460
If you don't want me
using your stuff, put a lock on it.

08:34.460 --> 08:35.980
What did you say?

08:37.590 --> 08:39.330
Where are my bananas?

08:40.430 --> 08:41.330
Right here.

08:41.330 --> 08:44.300
They weren't nearly sweet enough.

08:44.300 --> 08:46.880
I soaked them in sugar and honey.

08:46.880 --> 08:48.240
Apologize to my bananas!

08:48.240 --> 08:51.460
Bananas are a perfect and
flawless food the way they are!

08:51.460 --> 08:53.670
Banana is perfect!

08:54.670 --> 08:58.570
If you care about them so much, you
should lock them away somewhere.

08:58.570 --> 08:59.610
What?

08:59.610 --> 09:00.540
Ignorant peasant.

09:00.540 --> 09:02.770
Shut up, you sweet-toothed aristocrat.

09:02.770 --> 09:04.770
Quiet, dandelion head.

09:04.770 --> 09:06.700
What did you say?

09:06.700 --> 09:08.430
You're a wild dog that tries to bite everyone.

09:07.430 --> 09:10.430
They're so noisy.

09:08.430 --> 09:10.960
Well, so are you.

09:10.430 --> 09:11.690
Reiji, stop them.

09:10.960 --> 09:12.480
Silence, disgraced nobleman!

09:12.480 --> 09:14.670
What did you say, you sweets-addled moron?

09:14.670 --> 09:16.110
Reiji?

09:17.210 --> 09:19.030
Miss Nanami.

09:19.030 --> 09:24.160
I hired you to write all three
songs for the decisive concert.

09:25.140 --> 09:27.920
But I have another order for you, please.

09:29.210 --> 09:37.880
I'd like you to create the seven songs
for the STARISH and HEAVENS duet project!

09:40.330 --> 09:41.600
Yes, sir.

09:42.860 --> 09:45.640
I see. That sounds tough, Nanami.

09:45.640 --> 09:48.200
Haru-chan, do your best.

09:48.200 --> 09:49.210
I will.

09:49.210 --> 09:53.600
Nanami, you always pour your entire
being into everything you do.

09:53.600 --> 09:56.700
That's what makes
our little lamb so wonderful.

09:56.700 --> 10:00.690
I think it's a huge honor.

10:01.220 --> 10:02.200
And...

10:03.040 --> 10:06.410
I want to write songs for all of you.

10:06.410 --> 10:11.750
When I think someone else might be
writing songs for you, it makes me jealous.

10:13.090 --> 10:15.710
Nanami-san, you're unbelievable.

10:17.200 --> 10:20.790
I'm starting to get excited
about the duet project.

10:20.790 --> 10:23.540
I definitely want to sing
if it's a song you wrote, Nanami.

10:23.540 --> 10:26.270
Haruka, we'll support you
from the bottoms of our hearts.

10:26.270 --> 10:27.200
Thank you.

10:30.520 --> 10:32.440
What did you say, you rude fool?

10:32.440 --> 10:33.940
It's true.

10:33.940 --> 10:35.870
I've had enough of you.

10:35.870 --> 10:37.610
And I've had enough of you.

10:39.330 --> 10:40.750
You hooligan rocker.

10:40.010 --> 10:45.880
Ugh. On average, there's a problem
every 3 minutes and 47 seconds.

10:40.750 --> 10:44.700
I'm always telling you to
hang up your used washcloths.

10:44.700 --> 10:45.610
Shut up, you hungry hippo!

10:45.610 --> 10:48.340
Huh? Of course I'm hungry!

10:46.500 --> 10:48.790
Reiji, can't you do something?

10:48.340 --> 10:50.430
Then is there nothing in your head but food and rock?

10:50.430 --> 10:53.670
And do you ever think of anything but sweets?

10:50.430 --> 10:53.670
Hey, why have you been ignoring
them since yesterday?

10:54.130 --> 10:56.590
This is your fault.

10:57.800 --> 10:59.930
Yeah. It's your fault, Reiji.

11:01.090 --> 11:07.400
Yeah. If you hadn't suggested that we live
together, this wouldn't have happened.

11:15.710 --> 11:17.110
Hi.

11:19.360 --> 11:24.780
I see. You're on your way to a meeting
for QUARTET NIGHT's decisive concert song.

11:24.780 --> 11:30.290
Yeah. I was surprised to hear
they're living in a condo together.

11:31.460 --> 11:33.080
Rei-chan convinced them to do it.

11:33.490 --> 11:37.250
They were originally brought together
by Shiny, and I was like,

11:38.630 --> 11:43.090
"Wow! You're putting these
four together? How interesting!"

11:43.580 --> 11:48.390
They captured my interest,
but I thought it would never work.

11:48.950 --> 11:51.270
They seemed so incompatible.

11:52.760 --> 11:55.270
But they're still together.

11:56.250 --> 11:56.900
Yes.

11:56.900 --> 11:59.100
It's all thanks to Rei-chan.

11:59.100 --> 12:02.280
They made it this far because of him.

12:03.370 --> 12:05.450
And he's the reason they're still together.

12:06.810 --> 12:07.760
Hey.

12:07.760 --> 12:09.800
Why aren't you saying anything?

12:09.800 --> 12:11.450
Why don't you say something?

12:13.430 --> 12:16.630
I can't do this anymore.

12:24.950 --> 12:26.280
Let this be the end.

12:54.580 --> 12:57.290
What? Kotobuki-senpai did what?

12:57.290 --> 13:00.420
Didn't I just tell you that? He left.

13:00.420 --> 13:01.840
What? Um...

13:02.280 --> 13:04.470
He truly is self-centered.

13:04.470 --> 13:07.800
I can't believe he quit when
he's the one who suggested it.

13:08.120 --> 13:10.470
I wasn't expecting this, either.

13:11.930 --> 13:15.440
Um... I think we should
go look for him immediately.

13:15.440 --> 13:16.490
Leave him.

13:16.490 --> 13:18.730
There's no need to look for him.

13:18.730 --> 13:19.790
But...

13:20.410 --> 13:22.280
Reiji will come back soon.

13:23.610 --> 13:24.810
Okay.

13:24.810 --> 13:28.530
I know you came all the way here,
but we'll have to postpone today's meeting.

13:30.260 --> 13:30.870
Sorry.

13:37.500 --> 13:39.230
Kotobuki-senpai.

13:44.940 --> 13:46.170
Thanks for waiting.

13:48.050 --> 13:48.890
Coming.

13:50.930 --> 13:52.800
Let's try a different pose.

13:54.850 --> 13:56.740
Mikaze-san, you're up.

13:56.740 --> 13:57.520
Okay.

14:18.830 --> 14:21.200
Reiji's not back.

14:21.630 --> 14:23.210
You know him.

14:23.210 --> 14:27.130
Could he have returned already
and be hiding somewhere?

14:27.130 --> 14:29.800
I looked. I didn't find anything.

14:30.540 --> 14:31.970
Then where is he?

14:33.540 --> 14:34.680
I don't know.

14:35.420 --> 14:37.060
He's not answering his phone, either.

14:40.130 --> 14:43.420
This is the first time
he's done anything like this.

14:44.920 --> 14:45.400
Hyuga Ryuya

14:46.390 --> 14:48.110
Hyuga-san?

14:52.240 --> 14:54.030
Reiji called.

14:55.120 --> 14:57.400
He didn't sound like himself.

14:59.040 --> 15:01.080
Reiji? What's wrong?

15:01.410 --> 15:04.360
Ryuya-senpai, sorry.

15:05.000 --> 15:08.670
But I don't think I can do this anymore.

15:12.170 --> 15:14.890
Your individual talents are incredible.

15:15.260 --> 15:19.100
So is the way you're true
to yourselves in everything you do.

15:19.880 --> 15:21.190
But...

15:22.090 --> 15:25.110
Right now, you should be putting
all your efforts towards being a group.

15:26.540 --> 15:29.230
Sometimes you have to work
hard for the other members,

15:29.230 --> 15:31.050
even if it means sacrificing yourselves.

15:31.810 --> 15:34.030
So why are you so divided?

15:43.220 --> 15:45.840
You won't capture any hearts like that.

15:47.160 --> 15:49.110
Don't underestimate what it takes to be an idol!

16:04.620 --> 16:07.770
I've clashed with him in countless ways.

16:09.370 --> 16:12.070
I thought it didn't matter,
regardless of what I said.

16:13.150 --> 16:17.700
Without Reiji, we weren't a group.

16:22.400 --> 16:27.210
Starting today, the four of you will be moving,
moving as an idol group.

16:27.210 --> 16:28.160
What?

16:28.160 --> 16:29.420
Impossible.

16:29.420 --> 16:32.380
Objectively speaking, this is
the worst possible combination.

16:32.380 --> 16:34.420
What? But...

16:39.880 --> 16:41.440
What?

16:41.440 --> 16:43.250
You've been more than high-handed.

16:43.250 --> 16:46.520
Why did you bring us all the way out here?

16:48.530 --> 16:50.860
No matter how you look at it,
we're not a good match.

16:50.860 --> 16:51.690
Yeah.

16:51.690 --> 16:53.950
But we do agree on that.

16:55.230 --> 16:57.490
I get that we don't get along,
but don't be that way.

16:57.490 --> 17:00.260
Let's give it a shot.

17:00.260 --> 17:03.160
Shiny-san said we're a group now.

17:03.160 --> 17:04.830
It could be a good opportunity.

17:07.130 --> 17:11.130
If we really don't think it'll work,
then we'll just quit.

17:11.660 --> 17:14.200
Won't you be willing to try
if you approach it that way?

17:23.540 --> 17:25.560
Is that time now?

17:26.530 --> 17:30.400
But is it okay if things end like this?

17:31.300 --> 17:34.430
If Kotobuki doesn't want to,
then it can't be helped.

17:43.570 --> 17:45.380
That was just today.

17:45.380 --> 17:46.370
You're right.

17:46.370 --> 17:50.170
It wouldn't so bad if we stayed together.

17:58.100 --> 17:58.680
Hey.

17:59.620 --> 18:02.600
I hate everything you do.

18:02.960 --> 18:04.520
I could say the same thing.

18:04.520 --> 18:06.100
Hey, guys.

18:06.100 --> 18:11.720
But when we sing as QUARTET NIGHT, you're not bad.

18:12.220 --> 18:13.460
Neither are you.

18:13.460 --> 18:15.560
It's not so bad when we're singing together.

18:18.410 --> 18:20.410
We will never be friends.

18:20.410 --> 18:22.870
But we're comrades.

18:26.660 --> 18:28.910
It can't end like this.

18:28.910 --> 18:32.080
Yeah, not even if Kotobuki
doesn't want to continue.

18:32.080 --> 18:33.590
You're right.

18:33.590 --> 18:37.510
We should start moving forward together again.

18:50.860 --> 18:53.480
I believed you would come.

18:53.480 --> 18:54.920
Don't be ridiculous!

18:54.920 --> 18:56.700
Why would you do that?

18:56.700 --> 18:58.280
Were you testing us?

18:59.310 --> 19:00.990
No.

19:02.150 --> 19:04.080
I couldn't afford to do that.

19:05.850 --> 19:09.350
I really didn't think
I could keep going then.

19:10.200 --> 19:14.920
I forced us to live together, so we would bond.

19:16.210 --> 19:20.010
But when I thought my plan
backfired, I was terrified.

19:21.180 --> 19:26.500
Something I thought would
be good wasn't helping us.

19:30.320 --> 19:31.850
That's not true.

19:32.400 --> 19:37.350
Without you, we would've
parted ways long ago.

19:37.350 --> 19:38.190
Yeah.

19:40.630 --> 19:41.650
Bonds, huh?

19:43.790 --> 19:45.070
We've already got them.

19:45.070 --> 19:45.930
What?

19:45.930 --> 19:47.320
You're right.

19:47.320 --> 19:50.270
What do you think the odds are
that we would meet on this beach

19:50.270 --> 19:51.750
simply by coincidence?

20:08.300 --> 20:10.230
This is the bond between groupmates.

20:11.750 --> 20:15.900
Hey, guys. Why don't we ride this
momentum and go on a national tour?

20:16.350 --> 20:19.080
A national tour? Us?

20:19.080 --> 20:21.770
That doesn't sound like us, but...

20:22.360 --> 20:24.570
We'll consider it.

20:25.850 --> 20:27.030
Guys!

20:28.590 --> 20:31.960
Whoa whoa, whoa whoa

20:32.330 --> 20:33.830
Whoa whoa

20:36.110 --> 20:39.930
Whoa whoa, whoa whoa

20:39.930 --> 20:41.820
Whoa whoa

20:47.100 --> 20:50.010
The sky's awfully bright

20:50.010 --> 20:52.610
With only dreams in the trunk

20:52.610 --> 20:57.110
And nowhere to go

20:55.130 --> 20:57.110
However you wish, sing the song

20:57.110 --> 21:00.570
As we ride through the town

20:58.840 --> 21:02.150
Whoa whoa, whoa whoa

21:02.150 --> 21:05.150
Drawn together by something

21:05.150 --> 21:07.660
COLORING that doesn't match

21:07.660 --> 21:09.330
Mixing together and bursting apart

21:09.330 --> 21:15.580
Like the world's only contrarian blues

21:13.930 --> 21:17.290
Whoa whoa, whoa whoa

21:17.290 --> 21:21.130
Sometimes we cut so deep that it hurts

21:21.130 --> 21:24.550
Sometimes our feelings
fade away into the distance

21:24.550 --> 21:28.550
But our beating hearts can't be beaten

21:28.550 --> 21:33.150
The light we received keeps on shining

21:33.150 --> 21:36.910
Blown by the wind and entwined in our dreams

21:36.910 --> 21:42.050
The days we've always stood back to back

21:42.050 --> 21:48.230
Believing that's the answer

21:48.230 --> 21:52.070
Layering our songs and voices
on this trackless road

21:52.070 --> 21:56.720
Together, we light up the bonds between us

21:56.720 --> 22:03.090
The day we can call each other friend

22:03.090 --> 22:08.730
Is the day we'll take each other's hands

22:17.770 --> 22:20.360
The featured duet project.

22:20.360 --> 22:22.230
The first ones to perform will be...

22:22.690 --> 22:24.820
Ichinose Tokiya.

22:25.630 --> 22:27.420
And Otori Eiji.

24:06.420 --> 24:08.770
Don't miss our concert.

24:09.190 --> 24:10.420
Uta Pri!
